stty: add -F, whose settings stay until changed

On Linux, "stty -F /dev/ttyS1 9600 raw" sets up a serial port for the
programs that open it later. FreeBSD's stty has -f instead, and the
settings only last while the terminal is open: its first open starts
from the initial state, the .init device. OpenComputers II's serial
library and manual use "stty -F" to set up its serial interface card.

Add -F: as -f, and the settings also become the terminal's initial
state, when it has one.

